  "transcript": "Canonical serialisation rule: recursive descent through the proposal artifact, emitting all object keys in sorted (lexicographic) order, no whitespace, no newlines, UTF-8 bytes only. A third party reproduces hProposal by computing sha256(proposal_canon.json) where proposal_canon.json is the exact byte sequence of the canonically serialised proposal; then reproduces seedHex by computing sha256(hProposal || salt) where hProposal = 76059f5669efd54d274bd894cde6a3b6b80a5ccec8459ec2e332b2dae187176f and salt = d99062c76e64e73a73543e02c39e0a293d06be5db8f8d66c19aff60a17cfc1c2 concatenated as hex strings, hashed again with sha256 to yield 7af2a5718783c5bee6e511caddc5bdaf408af90d0b591c050783addff82c3e58."
